{"cross_mech":[],"family":{"alphafold_models":3590,"candidate_reasons":["pfam_previous_unknown_name"],"characterization_status":"","context_evidence_count":null,"cross_mech":{"example_proteins":0,"protein_traits_record":false,"records_by_mech":{},"scanned":false},"curation_status":"SEEDED","demotion_reasons":[],"description":"Anamorsin, subsequently named CIAPIN1 for cytokine-induced anti-apoptosis inhibitor 1, in humans is the homologue of yeast Dre2, a conserved soluble eukaryotic Fe-S cluster protein, that functions in cytosolic Fe-S protein biogenesis. It is found in both the cytoplasm and in the mitochondrial intermembrane space (IMS) [[cite:PUB00055951]]. CIAPIN1 is found to be up-regulated in hepatocellular cancer, is considered to be a downstream effector of the receptor tyrosine kinase-Ras signalling pathway, and is essential in mouse definitive haematopoiesis [[cite:PUB00055952]]. Dre2 has been found to interact with the yeast reductase Tah18, forming a tight cytosolic complex implicated in the response to high levels of oxidative stress [[cite:PUB00109169]]. These proteins consist of two domains, the N-terminal well-folded one, with a S-adenosylmethionine methyltransferase-like fold and the C-terminal more flexible domain, represented in this entry, which contains two highly conserved cysteine rich motifs that bind Fe-S clusters [[cite:PUB00067100],[cite:PUB00056284]].","domain_architectures":90,"interpro_id":"IPR046408","known_evidence_count":null,"matches":4936,"name":"Cytokine-induced anti-apoptosis inhibitor 1, Fe-S biogenesis","partial_evidence_count":null,"pfam_id":"PF05093","proteins":4152,"proteomes":3289,"short_name":"CIAPIN1","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/entry/pfam/PF05093","structures":0,"taxa":8763,"unknown_status":"EX_DUF"},"inputs":{"cross_mech":"cross-mech-duf-examples-2026-10-10","members":"pfam-uniprot-uniref90-2026-10-07","protein_examples":"duf-protein-examples-direct-2026-10-13","worklist":"interpro-pfam-duf-2026-10